<title>TURKEY: TURKEY'S HALKBANK TO LAUNCH $100-MLN SYDICATION.</title>
<headline>TURKEY'S HALKBANK TO LAUNCH $100-MLN SYDICATION.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state Halkbank will launch a $100 million syndication next week to be used for pre-export financing, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the bank might mandate ABCIC/ABC, Fuji, Sanwa, Credit Lyonnais, Standard Chartered, Sumitomo Bank and WestLB to co-arrange for the loan, but negotiations for more co-arrangers were under way.</p>
<p>They did not give other details.</p>
<p>--Ankara newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
